Z||000000||KnightRyder31||08-08-2000||11:39 AM||||Well, first of all, when I start my car(after it's been sitting) it likes to cough up smoke threw the exhaust pipes. Then, when I drive for over 10mins, and stop at a light...I see smoke(very light) coming out of the engine comp. The smoke doesn't smell like oil, it smells like rubber. Could this be a belt wearing? Also, it smokes(engine comp.) lightly after a shut the car off after a 10min+ drive. This is starting to make me worrie!!! Maybe I'm just paranoid?||||reg||11
Z||000001||80's BOY||08-08-2000||02:39 PM||||sounds like you may be slinging tranny fluid on your exhaust somewhere. check the seals around your axles and look under the car for the source of the smoke while it's running. if it's not oil then check the firewall to see if the wiring harness is touching the exhaust somewhere.||||reg||3
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||08-08-2000||08:49 PM||||Could it be my belt rubbing against the battery protecter? Or could my alternater belt be burning up?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ROB MAC||08-09-2000||11:09 AM||||If it is the plastic battery cover you will see the gouge marks and yes it stinks when it slowly disintegrates.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||08-09-2000||11:38 AM||||So that could wear on the belt. The alternater belt is already loose I think, because everytime I start up the car when Its been sitting for awhile, the damn thing squeels like a pig. Well, until the Voltometer goes to about 15...then it stops.<BR>You think maybe if I replaced and tightned my alternater belt, that this problem may stop?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||webbee||08-09-2000||03:18 PM||||Alt. belts are cheap and it's an easy job. I think that's your problem. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||webbee||08-09-2000||03:22 PM||||Alt. belts are cheap and it's an easy job. I think that's your problem. At least it will stop the squeel. You might check your pullys for distortion, too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||286SE'S||08-09-2000||04:05 PM||||The smoke from the exhaust at startup is a sign of worn valve guide seals. Oil seeps down the  valve stems while the car sits and it is burned into a nice stinky cloud. I have<BR>read that this is most common with the 2.5 engine but the 2.8 sometimes show it as well.<BR>It isn't a thing to worry about, my 2.5 SE has done it since I bought it 6 years ago with 72,000 miles on it.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
